      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The Voracious Angel Moth, of the Actias family, bears few similarities
    to its genus, with the only notable feature being their long-tailed hindwings.
    These moths lay their eggs in the corpses of other creatures, with the nutrients
    found in their decaying corpses aiding the gestation period. Because of these
    practices, it is fantasised that the pattern of their forewings (noted to look
    like several screaming, ghostly faces) is formed from the pain and suffering
    of the souls they feed on in their youth.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cdb2661bf4589ed468c40bf0073ce072, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1058936486334977727, guid: cdb2661bf4589ed468c40bf0073ce072,
